## ⚠️ Error Handling

### TRPCError Types

```typescript
throw new TRPCError({ code: 'UNAUTHORIZED', message: 'Invalid token' });
throw new TRPCError({ code: 'NOT_FOUND', message: 'User not found' });
```

### Client-Side Error Handling

```typescript
const { error } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['user', id], queryFn: () => trpc.user.getById.query(id) });
if (error) return <div>Error: {error.message}</div>;
```

---

## 🔒 Type Safety (End-to-End)

### Automatic Type Inference

```typescript
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['user', userId],
  queryFn: () => trpc.user.getById.query(userId),
});
// TypeScript knows data: User | undefined
```

### AppRouter Type Export

```typescript
export type AppRouter = typeof appRouter;
```

### Sharing Zod Schemas

```typescript
// shared/schemas/user.ts
export const createUserSchema = z.object({ email: z.string().email(), name: z.string() });
```

---

## 📚 Additional Resources

- **Official Documentation**: https://trpc.io/docs
- **GitHub Repository**: https://github.com/trpc/trpc

---

## 🎯 Best Practices Summary

### ✅ Do This

- ✅ Use `publicProcedure` for public endpoints
- ✅ Validate all inputs with Zod
- ✅ Organize routers by feature
- ✅ Use middleware for cross‑cutting concerns

### ❌ Avoid This

- ❌ Multiple tRPC instances
- ❌ Side effects in queries
- ❌ Generic error messages
- ❌ Importing server code on client

---

