# Full-Stack Type-Safe API with Express, Zod & React Query

This guide walks through building a type-safe API using **Express**, **Zod** for runtime validation, and **React Query** on the frontend. You'll get strong typing from shared schemas, but the client must define types manually – no automatic inference like tRPC, but with full control over your stack.

**Key Tradeoff**: Type safety is achieved via shared Zod schemas (published as a npm package), not automatic server-to-client inference. You'll write type definitions on both sides, but validation is unified.

---

## 🏗️ Project Structure

```
project/
├── shared/          # Shared Zod schemas & types
├── server/          # Express API
├── client/          # React + React Query
└── package.json
```

---

## 📦 Shared Schemas (Zod)

Define your data models once in a shared package, then import into both server and client.

```typescript
// shared/schemas/user.ts
import { z } from 'zod';

export const createUserSchema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email(),
  name: z.string().min(1),
});

export const updateUserSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string(),
  email: z.string().email().optional(),
  name: z.string().min(1).optional(),
});

export const userSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string(),
  email: z.string().email(),
  name: z.string(),
  createdAt: z.date(),
});

export type User = z.infer<typeof userSchema>;
export type CreateUserInput = z.infer<typeof createUserSchema>;
export type UpdateUserInput = z.infer<typeof updateUserSchema>;

// Pagination helper
export const paginationSchema = z.object({
  limit: z.number().min(1).max(100).default(10),
  cursor: z.string().optional(),
});
```

```typescript
// shared/schemas/post.ts
import { z } from 'zod';
import { userSchema } from './user';

export const createPostSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1),
  content: z.string(),
  authorId: z.string(),
});

export const listPostsSchema = z.object({
  userId: z.string().optional(),
  published: z.boolean().optional(),
});

export const postSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string(),
  title: z.string(),
  content: z.string(),
  authorId: z.string(),
  author: userSchema.nullable(),
  published: z.boolean(),
  createdAt: z.date(),
});

export type Post = z.infer<typeof postSchema>;
export type CreatePostInput = z.infer<typeof createPostSchema>;
```

Publish `shared` as a local package (e.g., `@myapp/shared`) to be consumed by both server and client.

